<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="021" project="reuse-governance-tightening-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Reviewer checks: capability duplication (F2) and requirements trace (F4)</title>
    <phase>3 Sweep and reviewer checks</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 001</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies an agent definition and task-execute under explicit project constraints (FR-07)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Wording that a fable reviewer will apply as a finding class must be precise; agent-definition authoring</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ — main-session-only (permission boundary)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add two checks to .claude/agents/adversarial-reviewer.md in one change: capability duplication against the capability index (F2 or K-class) and a per-criterion requirements trace when the caller supplies a POML or spec (F4 or K-class); make task-execute Step 9.5 pass the POML/spec path.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer maintaining agent definitions.</role>
  <goal>The reviewer definition carries both checks with finding classes matching task-execute's class table, tells callers to pass the POML/spec path, and task-execute Step 9.5 passes it.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-07; design.md sections 5.1 item 5 and 7.4. Items 3 and 5(d) edit the same file and land together.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">.claude/agents/adversarial-reviewer.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/patterns/CAPABILITY-INDEX.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="done">The index the duplication check reads</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Duplication check wording: new surface duplicating a capability in .claude/patterns/CAPABILITY-INDEX.md (same concept under another name, or a new package or service where the row says extend) is F2 when it adds a second implementation of an indexed capability, K-class when it is a judgment call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Trace check: when given a POML or spec.md, each acceptance criterion is reported as met (file:line plus test), not met (F4 when inside the change set's scope) or not verifiable from the diff (K-class with a reason).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Class names must match the F1-F4 / K1-K4 table in task-execute SKILL.md exactly; read it before writing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not change the reviewer's model, effort or tools frontmatter. In task-execute, change only the Step 9.5 reviewer-launch instruction (around line 463); no step renumbering.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/reuse-governance-tightening-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/agents/adversarial-reviewer.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Finding classes" location=".claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md">Step 9.5 finding triage: F1-F4 fix-now, K1-K4 known-limit.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the reviewer definition's Rules and Output sections and task-execute's class table.</step>
    <step order="2">Add both checks and the caller instruction to the reviewer definition.</step>
    <step order="3">Edit task-execute Step 9.5 so the reviewer launch passes the task POML path (and spec.md path when present).</step>
    <step order="4">Verify by one reviewer run on a small existing diff with its POML: the output contains a per-criterion trace. Record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the task-execute class table has no class matching "duplicates an existing mechanism" (F2) or "unmet acceptance criterion" (F4), STOP and escalate rather than inventing a class.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="Agent">adversarial-reviewer (fable) for the verification run</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">.claude/agents/adversarial-reviewer.md</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The reviewer definition contains both checks with the exact classes in the constraints.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The definition instructs callers to pass the POML/spec path; task-execute Step 9.5 passes it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">One verification run reports a per-criterion trace (recorded in notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: reviewer frontmatter unchanged; no task-execute step renumbered.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Lands in the items 1-3 PR (task 080).</notes>

  <completion-notes>Completed 2026-11-12. adversarial-reviewer.md: capability-duplication check (F2 for a second implementation of an indexed capability, K-class for a judgment call, row named either way); new Input section telling callers to pass the task POML and spec.md paths; requirements trace (met with file:line plus test / not met = F4 in scope / not verifiable from the diff = K-class with reason). Found and fixed in the same file: the Output class list described F1-F4 differently from the task-execute table (silent failure, a test that proves nothing, a contract break); it now names the table and its classes. Frontmatter unchanged. task-execute Step 9.5 review-scope rule 3 now launches the reviewer with the POML and spec paths. Deviation (directional): task-execute had no reviewer-launch line near 463; rule 3 is the only verifier-pass instruction, so the change went there. No other skill launches the reviewer. Verification run (adversarial-reviewer, fable, 88,744 tokens) on task 042 commit 9456083c78 with its POML and spec: per-criterion trace of 7 criteria (4 met, 1 met with a caveat, 2 not verifiable from the diff, with K4 reasons), capability duplication reported none, classes from the table. It found an F2 in merged task 042 (two live comments still saying CS0618 is downgraded); fixed on the branch with an optional K4 (SPRK001 example), and one K4 known limit recorded, see notes/042-cs0618.md. No step renumbered; skill-length guard 0 new; Test-InstructionPaths 0 new. rework: none task 021</completion-notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
